did\n\nAll three blocking rev3 findings are closed, plus all six non-blocking observations.\n\n**F2 — migration never carried a non-default member.** The reviewer was explicit that three cases for the three cited members would just re-create the defect, so the property has three coupled parts: `wireLeafTOMLPaths` derives the Configuration 1.0.0 member set from `reflect.TypeOf(rawV1{})`; a saturated fixture must cover every derived path at a value distinguishable from the one a dropped member decays to — where the decay oracle is a minimal v1 migrated through the real `Migrate`, since `currentWire` emits every member; and the *whole* loaded `Configuration` is compared before and after on `v1→2.0.0`, `2.0.0→3.0.0`, and a fresh direct `v1→3.0.0`. Ten members can't be saturated because the validators pin them to one value — each declares the alternate it claims is refused, and that alternate is driven through the real `Load`. Widening any of those six validators reddens the exemption self-check, so the exemption list can't outlive its justification.\n\n**F1** — full version cross-product at the real `AssessCompatibility` entry, versions from the pinned catalog, expected mode from a test-local major parse rather than the production `compareSemver` it bounds, and the test fails if either direction went unexercised.\n\n**F3** — the temp-file `Sync` is now countable and failable. Two injected-failure cases inherit the existing durability invariant set; the narrowing direction is pinned separately by `fileSyncCalls == createTempCalls`.\n\n## Sweep figure, stated honestly\n\n**73 mutants — 71 RED, 1 survivor, 1 positive control GREEN, 0 invalid.** The survivor is R13 and I'm reporting it as a survivor rather than folding it into the RED count. `encodeVersion2`'s directory-collection passthrough is unreachable from the only production call path, so the harness declares it in `EXPECT_SUBSUMED` with the subsuming check named, and prints `SUBSUMPTION CLAIM NO LONGER NEEDED` if it